REBOOT(1)                      P32W Unix                       REBOOT(1)

NAME
       reboot - restart the machine at once

SYNOPSIS
       reboot

DESCRIPTION
       reboot is for root. It calls sync(2), then the reboot(2)
       system call with RB_REBOOT, which writes every mounted
       filesystem out, marks each one clean, prints

              P32W Unix: rebooting

       on the console, stops the clock and jumps to address 0, as
       the reset button does: the boot monitor starts on the
       console. Type b there to boot P32W Unix again.

       No one is warned and no process is told: programs running
       on either terminal simply stop. Use shutdown -r to warn the
       users and end their processes first.

EXIT STATUS
       Only on failure: 1, with reboot: and the reason, if the
       caller is not root.

SEE ALSO
       halt(1), shutdown(1), sync(1), reboot(2), init(8)

BUGS
       There are no options. Data still buffered inside a running
       program (stdio) is lost.
